  "title": "JavaScript Typed Arrays",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Typed Arrays"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "Typed Arrays\nTyped arrays was designed for handling Binary Data.\nUnlike arrays, typed arrays are buffers of Fixed Length.\nTyped arrays store elements of Fixed Types like 8-bit integers or 32-bit numbers."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const myArr = new Uint8Array(5);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const myArr = new Uint8Array([0,1,2,3,4]);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const myArr = Uint8Array.of(0,1,2,3,4);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const myArr = Uint8Array.from([0,1,2,3,4]);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_uint8_1"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Typed Array Benefits"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Typed Arrays were designed to provide an efficient way to handle binary data,\nunlike traditional JavaScript arrays which can hold elements of mixed data types."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Typed arrays are raw memory, so JavaScript can pass them directly to any function\nwithout converting the data to another representation."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Typed arrays are seriously faster than normal arrays for passing data\nto functions that can use raw binary data. Typed Arrays are highly suitable for:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "WebGL and Canvas:\nFast graphics rendering and image processing.",
        "File APIs:\nFast reading and writing of local files.",
        "Media APIs:\nFast handling of audio and video data.",
        "WebSockets:\nEfficient binary data transfer over network."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Typed arrays provide a way to handle binary data as efficiently as arrays work in C."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Browser APIs Supporting Typed Arrays"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "fetch(url)\n\n.then(request => request.arrayBuffer())\n\n.then(arrayBuffer =>...);",
      "caption": "Fetch API Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const canvas = document.getElementById('my_canvas');\n\nconst context = canvas.getContext('2d');\n\nconst imageData = context.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n\nconst uint8ClampedArray = imageData.data;",
      "caption": "Canvas Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Differences from Regular Arrays"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Fixed Length:\nTyped Arrays cannot be dynamically resized using methods like push() or pop().",
        "Type Restriction:\nElements must adhere to the specified data type of the typed array.",
        "Underlying Buffer:\nTyped Arrays are views into an ArrayBuffer, allowing direct manipulation of binary data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Typed Array Types"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Name", "Min", "Max", "Bytes", "Type"],
        ["Int8Array", "-128", "127", "1", "byte"],
        ["Uint8Array", "0", "255", "1", "octet"],
        ["Uint8ClampedArray", "0", "255", "1", "octet"],
        ["Int16Array", "-32768", "32767", "2", "short"],
        ["Uint16Array", "0", "65535", "2", "unsigned short"],
        ["Int32Array", "-2147483648", "2147483647", "4", "long"],
        ["Uint32Array", "0", "4294967295", "4", "unsigned long"],
        ["BigInt64Array", "-263", "263 - 1", "8", "bigint"],
        ["BigUint64Array", "0", "264 - 1", "8", "unsigned bigint"],
        ["", "", "", "", ""],
        ["Float16Array", "-65504", "65504", "2", "unrestricted half"],
        ["Float32Array", "-3.4e38", "3.4e38", "4", "unrestricted float"],
        ["Float64Array", "-1.8e308", "1.8e308", "8", "unrestricted double"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "8 Bit Integers"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Name", "Data Type", "Range"],
      "rows": [
        ["Int8Array", "Signed integer (byte)", "-128/127"],
        ["Uint8Array", "Unsigned integer (octet)", "0/255"],
        ["Uint8ClampedArray", "Unsigned integer (octet)", "0/255"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const myArr = new Int8Array(10);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const myArr = new Uint8Array(10);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const myArr = new Uint8ClampedArray(10);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_typed_int8"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Uint8Array vs Uint8ClampedArray"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The difference between an Uint8Array and  an Uint8ClampedArray is how values are added."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If you set one element in an Uint8ClampedArray to a value outside the 0-255 range,\nit will default to 0 or 255."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A typed array will just take the first 8 bits of the value."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Typed arrays are not arrays."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "isArray() on a typed array returns false."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Many array methods (like push and pop) are not supported by typed arrays."
    },
